# Tracer: a selected conclusion keeps the identity and location of its complete source fact.
#
# Before: instantiating the second conclusion of a multi-conclusion `forall`
# could synthesize a one-conclusion source, so its FactId no longer identified
# the fact that had actually been stored.
#
# Now: `$second_property(2)` cites `paired_source` together with conclusion
# location 1; downstream result consumers can project that exact conclusion
# from the complete two-conclusion source.
#
# Boundary: alpha-equivalent binder spellings may share a proposition lookup,
# but a FactId may never be redirected to a different proposition. The latter
# fail-closed boundary is covered by the paired Rust regression test.
#
abstract_prop first_property(x)
abstract_prop second_property(x)

axiom paired_source:
    ? forall x R:
        $first_property(x)
        $second_property(x)

$second_property(2)
